# Copied to .env by `make dev-venv`. Read by docker compose AND by honcho, so
# the container stack and the ad-hoc host processes agree on every port.
#
# Container stack (docker compose): host ports. Defaults avoid the ports the
# main stack uses, so a worktree can run beside it.
ODL_API_PORT=18001
ODL_DASHBOARD_PORT=8081
ODL_PATCHING_PORT=18011
ODL_MCP_PORT=18081
ODL_N8N_PORT=5679
ODL_REDIS_PORT=16379

# Ad-hoc host processes (honcho): the hot-reloading read-only API, the Vite
# dev server, the MCP server.
DEV_API_PORT=18002
DEV_UI_PORT=5174
DEV_MCP_PORT=18082

# ---- Redis --------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the fleet state lives. Leave unset to use the local Redis on
# ODL_REDIS_PORT (the compose container, or redis-server from Procfile.local).
# Any redis-py URL works: redis://host:6379/0, redis://:password@host:6379/0,
# redis://user:password@host:6379/0, rediss://user:password@host:6380/0 (TLS).
# REDIS_URL=rediss://odl:change-me@redis.example.internal:6380/0
# Password only (requirepass): redis://:PASSWORD@host:6379/0
# ACL user + password:         redis://USER:PASSWORD@host:6379/0
# TLS with a private CA:       rediss://USER:PASSWORD@host:6380/0?ssl_cert_reqs=required&ssl_ca_certs=/path/ca.pem
# URL-encode special characters in the password (@ %40, # %23, / %2F, : %3A).
# `make redis-ping` verifies the string without printing it.
# Key prefix, in case the instance is shared, and how long a cluster that is
# never collected again stays visible (seconds, 0 = forever).
# REDIS_PREFIX=odl
# REDIS_TTL_SECONDS=86400

# ---- Clusters (no-Docker mode, `make local`) ------------------------------
# The fleet config, relative to data-layer/ (both files are git-ignored):
#   config/acm.yaml       a static list of ACM hubs; ManagedClusters are discovered
#                         (copy data-layer/config/acm.example.yaml)
#   config/clusters.yaml  a direct list of OCP API endpoints
#                         (copy data-layer/config/clusters.example.yaml)
# ODL_CONFIG=config/acm.yaml
# Credentials the config references as ${VAR} (any string in the config may be
# a ${VAR}: username, password, token, api_url, ca_cert path):
# OCP_USERNAME=svc-ops-data
# OCP_PASSWORD=
# Application ownership from a registry file instead of labels: set
# applications.source: mapping in the manifest and point at the export
# (default config/app-map.json next to the manifest; see app-map.example.json).
# ODL_APP_MAP=/path/to/app-map.json
# Set false to run a read-only API against a Redis another instance fills.
# COLLECTOR_ENABLED=true
# REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECONDS=120
# Sweep speed: clusters collected in parallel, and resource kinds fetched in
# parallel within each cluster. The honcho log prints one line per cluster per
# sweep with the slowest kinds; GET /api/manifest/availability has the same per
# kind. Raise these first when sweeps are slow; disable heavy kinds (secrets,
# configmaps, events) in the manifest if they dominate and you do not need them.
# COLLECT_WORKERS=8          # clusters in flight per instance (each holds one cluster's raw JSON)
# COLLECT_FETCH_WORKERS=6    # kinds fetched in parallel within a cluster
# LIST_PAGE_SIZE=500
# Many clusters behind one hub: run several collector processes, each taking a
# slice of the fleet ("i/n", 0-based) against the same Redis; shard 0 does the
# end-of-sweep housekeeping. e.g. three terminals:
#   COLLECT_SHARD=0/3 DEV_API_PORT=18002 make local-api
#   COLLECT_SHARD=1/3 DEV_API_PORT=18003 make local-api
#   COLLECT_SHARD=2/3 DEV_API_PORT=18004 make local-api
# COLLECT_SHARD=

# Only needed for POST /api/query/ask (natural-language questions). Everything
# else, including POST /api/query/sql, works without it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
